            "id": "evt_b6d064146ab64ca0a459419b59348012",
            "kind": "plan",
            "source": "agent",
            "timestamp": "2026-06-11T05:15:41.682958Z",
            "schema_version": 1,
            "seq": 8,
            "meta": {},
            "summary": "Build a sensor dashboard with a Python API (port 3000) serving CSV-as-JSON and a Vite+React frontend (port 8000) showing a data table and summary card.",
            "steps": [
                {
                    "title": "Create Python backend API",
                    "detail": "Write a lightweight Python script using the built-in `http.server` module (no pip installs needed) that reads `uploads/sensor_readings.csv`, parses it with the `csv` module, and serves it as JSON at `GET /api/readings` on port 3000. It will also enable CORS so the React dev server can fetch it."
                },
                {
                    "title": "Scaffold Vite + React frontend",
                    "detail": "Run `npm create vite@latest frontend -- --template react` to bootstrap a React app, then install dependencies. Configure `vite.config.js` with a proxy so `/api/readings` requests from the dev server forward to `http://localhost:3000`."
                },
                {
                    "title": "Build dashboard UI components",
                    "detail": "Replace the default App with a dashboard that fetches `/api/readings`, renders a scrollable table (timestamp, sensor, temperature), and a summary card showing count, min temperature, and max temperature. Add basic CSS for a clean layout."
                },
                {
                    "title": "Start both servers and verify in browser",
                    "detail": "Launch the Python API on port 3000, then start the Vite dev server on port 8000. Open the preview to confirm the table and summary card render correctly with live data."
                }
            ],
            "revision": 1,
            "context": "## What I found\n\n- **CSV data**: `uploads/sensor_readings.csv` \u2014 200 rows, 3 columns (`timestamp`, `sensor`, `temperature_c`). Sensors include nvme, amdgpu, k10temp, spd5118. Temperatures range roughly 32\u201363\u00b0C.\n- **Workspace**: Empty aside from the uploaded CSV \u2014 fresh start, no existing code.\n\n## Approach\n\n- **Backend**: Python's stdlib `http.server` + `csv` \u2014 zero external dependencies, simple and reliable for serving static CSV as JSON.\n- **Frontend**: Vite + React (the standard modern stack). Vite's built-in proxy will forward `/api/*` to port 3000, avoiding CORS issues during dev.\n- **Ports**: Backend on 3000, frontend on 8000 (matching the preview port).\n\n## Trade-offs\n\n- No database or persistence \u2014 the CSV is read once at startup. Fine for this dashboard scope.\n- Using Python stdlib instead of Flask/FastAPI avoids a pip install step and keeps things minimal."
        },
        {
